SOURCE VERIFICATION — "NO interrupts firing" is FALSE (scout's self-report CONFIRMED)
  grep -rn "exit_boot_services|ExitBootServices|raise_tpl|Tpl::|disable_interrupt" aegis-uefi/src/
  -> ZERO matches. UEFI Boot Services are never exited, TPL is never raised.
  uefi::boot::stall is used at aegis-uefi/src/main.rs:79,158,245,398,406,414,675,766,824,881
  -> the firmware timer interrupt is live throughout the measurement.
  CONSEQUENCE: the bare-metal warm-pair 0.0067% was achieved WITH interrupts
  enabled. "No interrupts" is therefore not the mechanism. The mechanism is
  frequency pinned at ratio 25 + single-threaded + no other runnable task +
  arena allocation (no faults) + no hypervisor.

SOURCE VERIFICATION — the two settled negatives were NOT measured on the noisy arm
  aegis-core/benches/lut_mpgemm.rs:238-244  -> warm call, then "best of 5"
  aegis-core/benches/ctz_vs_simd.rs:161-185 -> warm calls, then INTERLEAVED
